msgid "Motor and Servo Connections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:7
#: 6948acd6337a4cf28a850700ca38f344
msgid "Two steering/throttle methods are supported and each requires slightly different wiring and configuration as described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:10
#: 55fa65ecf3164359a97bf102a72e188f
msgid "Separate Steering and Throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:12
#: f12663ec3507478eb56f51e4a5603c0d
msgid "Most RC cars are like full sized cars in that they have separate steering and throttle controls. For these rovers, the steering servo (which normally turns the front wheels) should be connected to the autopilot's RC Output 1.  The motor's ESC (which normally controls the speed of the back wheels) should be connected to RC Output 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:18
#: c7f2be5e6ec84e6894f8a37d868d6c63
msgid "For this setup these parameters values should be set (they should actually be set by default).  More details can be found on the :ref:`Motor and Servo Configuration <rover-motor-and-servo-configuration>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:20
#: d93f47f85f9a40689a133bd64da38d46
msgid ":ref:`SERVO1_FUNCTION <SERVO1_FUNCTION>` = 26 (Ground Steering)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:21
#: 695ba942f53a4ceab4d373f3d5c3f37b
msgid ":ref:`SERVO3_FUNCTION <SERVO3_FUNCTION>` = 70 (Throttle)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:26
#: 2b661352bc8c42929c6c3e32bcaa5ec0
msgid "Skid Steering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:28
#: 1917834cf37d462581a70d7907008ef6
msgid "\"Skid steering\" vehicles (like R2D2) control their direction and forward/reverse motions by varying the speed of two (or more) independent wheels.  For these style rovers the left wheel should be connected to RC Output 1 and the right wheel should be connected to RC Output 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:33
#: dbd6e79288b145b28317d26bf01aadd0
msgid "For this setup these parameters values will need to be set.  More details can be found on the :ref:`Motor and Servo Configuration <rover-motor-and-servo-configuration>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:35
#: 071073814bfc46baaf950e5da84d5c7f
msgid ":ref:`SERVO1_FUNCTION <SERVO1_FUNCTION>` = 73 (Throttle Left)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:36
#: 6b065cd546674acd89b7d9d1c42cb1f8
msgid ":ref:`SERVO3_FUNCTION <SERVO3_FUNCTION>` = 74 (Throttle Right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:39
#: 0a3ee40193ee4fc8ab4faf8150688c55
msgid "Omni Vehicles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:41
#: 094cb70fd4164f2ba6d8753bf52425dd
msgid "Omni vehicles can move laterally (i.e. left and right) without changing their heading with the help of omni wheels (`like these from RobotShop <https://www.robotshop.com/en/6-duraomni-wheel.html>`__) or thrusters.  ArduPilot supports three configurations X, Plus and \"3\".  The autopilot motor outputs that should be connected to each motor are shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-connections.rst:46
#: 66e606448f704c8aad6a3e7fd79ab513
msgid "Another style of wheel is Mecanum (`like these from RobotShop <https://www.robotshop.com/products/80mm-right-mecanum-wheel>`__). For these wheels, the autopilot motor outputs that should be connected to each motor are shown below."
msgstr ""

